<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baja California</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lower California</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> is the long peninsula of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a> and the Gulf of California. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missionaries began Spanish settlement at Loreto in 1697, and the territory was administered as a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>, separated from Alta California in 1804. In 1853 the American filibuster <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-walker">William Walker</a> briefly proclaimed an independent republic there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baja-california.jpg" alt="Baja California" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heraldry · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Baja_California.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
